<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paramaribo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paramaribo is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname-river">Suriname River</a> near the Atlantic coast. It grew around Fort Zeelandia as the administrative and commercial centre of the English and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> plantation colony. Its historic inner city of wooden colonial buildings was inscribed on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> World Heritage List in 2002, and about half of the country's population lives in and around it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paramaribo.jpg" alt="Paramaribo" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LLs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paramaribo_city_collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
